{
 "esm": "1.0.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "nr-airtoxics-lawn-garden-county",
  "description": "THE FIXTURE FOR THE LAST TWO NONROAD CALCULATORS. It computes all 14,036 MOVESOutput rows of the nr-airtoxics-lawn-garden-county snapshot -- 29 pollutant-processes over 484 (SCC, model year) cohorts -- from that snapshot's own input tables: the whole NONROAD exhaust chain over the Lawn/Garden sector's 108 equipment points, then NRHCSpeciationCalculator's five species, NRAirToxicsCalculator's twenty toxics and its separate NonHAPTOG pass. docs/nr-airtoxics-lawn-garden-county.md is the specification; run-nr-airtoxics-oracle.sh is an independent reproduction of the same 14,036 rows by a different route.\n\nIT BEGAN AS fixtures/nr-logging-county.esm WITH ITS PATHS CHANGED, which docs/esm-conventions.md 27.3 makes the first move on a new rung, and the retarget audit found three things that fixture could not have seen (specification 2.1). The largest: nremissionrate's three-level SCC fallback chain is walked once per (technology, pollutant-process), not once per equipment point -- a specific SCC's rate rows need not cover every technology its own tech mix names. Resolved per point instead, this document emits exactly the right 14,036-row key set and is wrong by up to a factor of 6.9 on five of the 31 SCCs. The other two: the .TECH hp bin is the FIRST containing bin and not every containing one, which a strict lower bound reproduces because the bins tile from 0; and a (pollutant-process, technology) pair with no nrdeterioration row takes a factor of 1 rather than 0, which 101 and 10001 never notice and 9901 -- which has no row anywhere in that table -- would be deleted by.\n\nWHAT THIS DOCUMENT DOES NOT CONTAIN, because the snapshot cannot show it (docs/esm-conventions.md 23, 36):\n\n* POLLUTANTS 131 AND 142 ARE EMITTED AND NOT COMPARED. Their 968 cells are computed by the same expression as every other toxic, from nrDioxinEmissionRate.meanBaseRate -- which this corpus's capture stores at twelve decimal places, so the rates 1.105e-09 and 1.9e-11 keep FOUR and TWO significant figures against the double MOVES read. Fitting the rate the reference must have used gives 1.1045021e-09 and 1.9434497e-11, both inside half a stored quantum of the captured value: that is the whole of the difference and no implementation reading this capture can be closer. tolerance.toml carries the exclusion as a SCOPE with the measurement, which is neither a widened tolerance nor a shortfall (36.3), and compare-output.py prints what it held out and why on every run.\n\n* NEITHER CALCULATOR'S MISSING-ROW ARM FIRES. Over all 2,063 (SCC, model year, technology, hp bin) worker cells this run produces there are 0 with no nrhpcategory row, 0 with no nrMethaneTHCRatio row and 0 with no nrHCSpeciation row -- so the Go's skip-the-emission and its explicit-zero fallback are written from the source and exercised only in components/nr_hc_speciation.esm, where a probe technology takes each.\n\n* THE TWO FUEL-SUBTYPE IDS CANNOT BE TOLD APART. nrMethaneTHCRatio and nrATRatio key on the fuel FORMULATION's subtype and nrHCSpeciation on the EMISSION's; the only supplied gasoline formulation carries 12 in both, so the distinction is preserved from the source and is unfalsifiable here.\n\n* THE MARKET-SHARE FAN-OUT IS 1.0 AND 0.0. Two formulations are supplied and one has share 0, so the per-formulation chain is collapsed at its two endpoints only. The general form -- the mean of the products rather than the product of the means (32.3) -- is written and untested.\n\n* MXTECH = 32 NEVER BITES. The largest .TECH technology list any of the 108 points draws is 9. The truncation is in the reference and is not in this document, and a sector that needed it would be wrong here.\n\n* ONE PROCESS, ONE FUEL TYPE. Everything is running exhaust and gasoline, so the fuel path's process-1-only guard is satisfied trivially and the diesel, CNG and LPG densities and the diesel PM2.5 fraction are never evaluated. The five ratio tables' output-pollutant sets are disjoint here, so the Go's last-write-wins overwrite is written and untested.\n\nTHE PRECISION IS THE REFERENCE'S: domain.element_type Float32 with a Float64 override on every SCC-valued variable, because 2260004015 is 135x binary32's exact-integer limit and would round into a different equipment category (finding F18). 17.2's rule -- one operator, one precision -- is why the speciation identifiers are Float32: they are all below 2^24.",
  "authors": [
   "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
  ],
  "tags": [
   "moves",
   "nonroad",
   "air-toxics",
   "speciation",
   "fixture"
  ]
 },
 "domain": {
  "element_type": "Float32"
 },
