    },
    {
     "_comment": "agedist.rs:133-136. A recurrence of lag 1: the MINGRWIND floor is applied to the RUNNING TOTAL before the year's factor and only when that factor is non-zero, and the clamp at zero is applied after. Either one the other way round is a different projection for a state with almost no equipment.",
     "lhs": "fold_totalPopulation",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "args": [],
      "output_idx": [
       "r",
       "w"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "r": {
        "from": "equipment_point_rows"
       },
       "w": {
        "from": "fold_year_rows"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "<=",
         "args": [
          "w",
          1
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "point_statePopulation",
          "r"
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "max",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "*",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "ifelse",
             "args": [
              {
               "op": "!=",
               "args": [
                {
                 "op": "index",
                 "args": [
                  "fold_annualGrowthFactor",
                  "r",
                  "w"
                 ]
                },
                0.0
               ]
              },
              {
               "op": "max",
               "args": [
                {
                 "op": "index",
                 "args": [
                  "fold_totalPopulation",
                  "r",
                  {
                   "op": "-",
                   "args": [
                    "w",
                    1
                   ]
                  }
                 ]
                },
                "minimumGrowthPopulation"
               ]
              },
              {
               "op": "index",
               "args": [
                "fold_totalPopulation",
                "r",
                {
                 "op": "-",
                 "args": [
                  "w",
                  1
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "op": "+",
             "args": [
              1.0,
              {
               "op": "index",
               "args": [
                "fold_annualGrowthFactor",
                "r",
                "w"
               ]
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          0.0
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "fold_residualMinuend",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "args": [],
      "output_idx": [
       "r",
       "w"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "r": {
        "from": "equipment_point_rows"
       },
       "w": {
        "from": "fold_year_rows"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "<=",
         "args": [
          "w",
          1
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "slot_baseModelYearFraction",
          "r",
          1
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "ifelse",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": ">",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "index",
             "args": [
              "point_statePopulation",
              "r"
             ]
            },
            0.0
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "/",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "index",
             "args": [
              "fold_totalPopulation",
              "r",
              "w"
             ]
            },
            {
             "op": "index",
             "args": [
              "point_statePopulation",
              "r"
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          0.0
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     },
     "_comment": "agedist.f's totpop/baspop, guarded by a VALUE rather than by a presence factor: eleven of this run's equipment points carry a base-year population of exactly 0, prccty.f skips them, and 0/0 is a NaN that no multiplicative mask downstream can remove."
    },
    {
     "_comment": "THE FOLD (\u00a72.2(e)), as esm-spec \u00a74.3.1.1's causal self-reference. The body reads `index(fold_scrappedFraction, r, w - a)`: itself, strictly earlier along the fold-year axis, with the equipment-point axis an identity index. The 51-slot vector fold is reduced to this scalar recurrence on 31 residuals first -- every cell of the grown vector is a clamped base times an ASCENDING run of survival factors, so slot `a` of year `w` traces back `a` years to the residual of year `w - a`, or to the 1990 vector if the fold has not run that long. tools/verify-agedist-reduction.py checks that reduction cell by cell in float32 against the specification's own script, 0 of 1,581 cells differing, on all six of the snapshot's equipment points. Two orders are load-bearing and both were measured: the residual is `minuend - sum` with the cohorts summed ascending FIRST (folding the negated terms into the minuend one at a time moves the answer up to 1.1e-05 relative, because the residual is a catastrophic cancellation), and each cohort's factors multiply left to right starting FROM the base (precomputing the run product moves it up to 6.4e-06).",
     "lhs": "fold_scrappedFraction",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "args": [],
      "output_idx": [
       "r",
       "w"
      ],
      "reduce": "+",
      "ranges": {
       "r": {
        "from": "equipment_point_rows"
       },
       "w": {
        "from": "fold_year_rows"
       },
       "a": [
        1,
        50
       ]
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "<=",
         "args": [
          "w",
          1
         ]
        },
        0.0,
        {
         "op": "apply_expression_template",
         "args": [],
         "name": "agedist_cohort_term",
         "bindings": {
          "equipment_point": "r",
          "fold_year": "w",
          "age_slot": "a",
          "survival": "slot_survivalFraction",
          "base_fraction": "slot_baseModelYearFraction",
          "residual_minuend": "fold_residualMinuend",
          "scrapped_sum": "fold_scrappedFraction"
         }
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "fold_newestCohortResidual",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "args": [],
      "output_idx": [
       "r",
       "w"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "r": {
        "from": "equipment_point_rows"
       },
       "w": {
        "from": "fold_year_rows"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "-",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "fold_residualMinuend",
          "r",
          "w"
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "fold_scrappedFraction",
          "r",
          "w"
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "The last fold row's vector, read back. `31` is the last row of fold_year_rows, the episode year: fold_yearID row 31 is asserted to be 2020 so the literal cannot drift away from the axis.",
     "lhs": "slot_grownModelYearFraction",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "args": [],
      "output_idx": [
       "r",
       "s"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "r": {
        "from": "equipment_point_rows"
       },
       "s": {
        "from": "age_slot_rows"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "<=",
         "args": [
          "s",
          1
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "fold_newestCohortResidual",
          "r",
          31
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "apply_expression_template",
         "args": [],
         "name": "agedist_cohort_term",
         "bindings": {
          "equipment_point": "r",
          "fold_year": 31,
          "age_slot": {
           "op": "-",
           "args": [
            "s",
            1
           ]
          },
          "survival": "slot_survivalFraction",
          "base_fraction": "slot_baseModelYearFraction",
          "residual_minuend": "fold_residualMinuend",
          "scrapped_sum": "fold_scrappedFraction"
         }
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "The skip as a membership test on a rectangular axis, which is what lets a ragged key set be produced without a ragged index set.",
     "lhs": "slot_isPopulated",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "args": [],
      "output_idx": [
       "r",
       "s"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "r": {
        "from": "equipment_point_rows"
       },
       "s": {
        "from": "age_slot_rows"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "and",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "<=",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "index",
             "args": [
              "slot_ageID",
              "s"
