       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "slot_detAge",
        "r",
        "s"
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "The technology code space, enumerated. Nothing is read here; it is the axis at which the next three equations meet.",
     "lhs": "tech_engTechID",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "args": [],
      "output_idx": [
       "c"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "c": {
        "from": "engine_tech_rows"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "+",
       "args": [
        99,
        "c"
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "J11. The .TECH rows the equipment chain, the hp bin, the exhaust process group and the cohort's mix year select, laid out per technology. THE ORDER OF THE `join` CLAUSES BELOW IS A COST DECISION AND NOT A READING ORDER -- docs/esm-conventions.md \u00a725, docs/findings/README.md F17. Only the FIRST clause a binding can resolve DRIVES enumeration; the other three still restrict the admitted set, but as per-leaf equality tests (CONFORMANCE_SPEC \u00a75.5.8, `the others are membership tests on the driven leaves`). This node therefore costs exactly what the first clause's match set admits, and every order gives byte-identical rows. Measured on the whole document, one `esm simulate --time 0` each: engTechID first admits 2,320,704 leaves and runs in 11.5 s; SCC first 5,977,200 and 20.4 s; modelYearID first 24,107,900 and 57.2 s; processGroupID first -- a key with TWO distinct values -- 272,523,600 and 541 s. Do not reorder these for legibility. THE LOWER HP BOUND IS STRICT, and that is docs/nr-airtoxics-lawn-garden-county.md 2.1(b): nonroad_loader.rs takes the FIRST (SCC, hpMin, hpMax) bin containing hpAvg, and `hpMin <= hpAvg` admits two of them wherever hpAvg sits on a bin boundary -- 2260004071's 3.0 hp is in both (1, 3) and (3, 6) of 2260000000. The bins tile from 0 and every hpAvg is positive, so the strict bound picks exactly the reference's bin; measured over all 108 points at all three chain levels, 0 differences. Without it tech_fractionTotal is 2 on that SCC and its emissions are 1.24 to 1.43 times the reference's.",
     "lhs": "tech_fraction",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "args": [],
      "semiring": "sum_product",
      "output_idx": [
       "c",
       "cc"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "c": {
        "from": "cohort_rows"
       },
       "m": {
        "from": "nrengtechfraction_rows"
       },
       "x": {
        "from": "exhaust_process_group_rows"
       },
       "cc": {
        "from": "engine_tech_rows"
       }
      },
      "join": [
       {
        "on": [
         [
          "tech_engTechID",
          "mix_engTechID"
         ]
        ]
       },
       {
        "on": [
         [
          "cohort_mixEffectiveSCC",
          "mix_SCC"
         ]
        ]
       },
       {
        "on": [
         [
          "mix_processGroupID",
          "epg_processGroupID"
         ]
        ]
       },
       {
        "on": [
         [
          "cohort_mixYearID",
          "mix_modelYearID"
         ]
        ]
       }
      ],
      "filter": {
       "op": "and",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "<",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "mix_hpMin",
            "m"
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "cohort_hpAvg",
            "c"
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": ">=",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "mix_hpMax",
            "m"
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "cohort_hpAvg",
            "c"
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "mix_fraction",
        "m"
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "tech_fractionTotal",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "args": [],
      "semiring": "sum_product",
      "output_idx": [
       "c"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "c": {
        "from": "cohort_rows"
       },
       "cc": {
        "from": "engine_tech_rows"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "tech_fraction",
        "c",
        "cc"
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "_comment": "J14, on the composite key, hoisted off the cohort axis: the table is keyed by (polProcessID, engTechID) and nothing else, so the age is the only part of the deterioration factor a cohort contributes.",
     "lhs": "det_isPresent",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "args": [],
      "semiring": "bool_and_or",
      "output_idx": [
       "q3",
